  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Trump and Mamdani appear friendly after ‘wide-ranging’ meeting at Gracie Mansion",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/21/trump-and-mamdani-meeting-gracie-mansion",
      "description": "<p>Republican president said he hoped the democratic socialist would be a ‘great mayor’ for New York City</p><p>Donald Trump said on Monday that he hoped Zohran Mamdani would be a “great mayor” for New York, an unusually warm assessment of the democratic socialist leader whom the president and his Republican allies have spent months holding up as a symbol of the Democratic party’s alleged embrace of “communism” ahead of the November midterms.</p><p>At a news conference following their closed-door meeting at Gracie Mansion, Trump and Mamdani appeared friendly as they have in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/nov/21/trump-mamdani-white-house-new-york\">previous</a> meetings. Mamdani said he and Trump held a “wide-ranging” discussion, which touched on affordable housing and immigration, but did not offer extensive details regarding any disagreements between them.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/21/trump-and-mamdani-meeting-gracie-mansion\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-22T01:30:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mamdani challenges Trump over White House press ban during meeting",
